		<!-- ============ MARKET UPDATE ============ -->
		<section class="market">
			<div class="wrap">
				<div class="eyebrow red reveal">Market update</div>
				<h2 class="display reveal" style="font-size:clamp(30px,3.8vw,48px)">What is the Northwest Houston market doing <em>right now?</em></h2>
				<p class="lede reveal">Greater Houston is a balanced market in mid-2026. The median single-family
					price held at $345,000 in June, homes averaged 52 days on market, and inventory sat at 5.2 months
					of supply, inside the 4-to-6-month range economists call balanced.</p>
				<p class="src-note reveal">Source: Houston Association of Realtors, June 2026 market update.</p>
				<div class="market-grid">
					<div class="mkt reveal"><div class="num">$345,000</div><div class="lbl">Houston median price · June 2026</div></div>
					<div class="mkt reveal"><div class="num">52 days</div><div class="lbl">Average time on market</div></div>
					<div class="mkt reveal"><div class="num">5.2 mo</div><div class="lbl">Months of supply</div></div>
					<div class="mkt dark-tile reveal"><div class="num">+12.3%</div><div class="lbl">Pending sales, year over year</div></div>
				</div>
				<div class="market-body">
					<p class="reveal">In Cypress, the median listing price was $435,535 in May 2026, with about 2,045
						homes for sale and a 35-day median time on market. Homes sold at roughly 98% of asking
						(Realtor.com Economic Research). Buyer demand has not disappeared: Houston pending sales rose
						12.3% year over year in June. But buyers have more choices than they did two years ago.</p>
					<p class="takeaway reveal">What that means for you: pricing precision matters more now than it did
						in 2021. Homes priced at or just below recent comparable sales still move. Overpriced listings sit.
						Every Lippincott Team listing starts with a data-backed pricing analysis.
						<a class="link-arrow" style="display:inline-block;margin-top:12px" href="https://www.thelippincottteam.com/sellers/pricing-your-home/"><em>See what your home is worth →</em></a></p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============ FSBO ============ -->
		<section class="fsbo">
			<div class="wrap">
				<h2 class="display reveal" style="font-size:clamp(30px,3.8vw,48px)">Should you sell with an agent or <em>on your own?</em></h2>
				<p class="lede reveal">Nationwide, the price gap between selling with an agent and selling on
					your own is measurable, and the hard parts owners run into alone are well documented:</p>
				<div class="fsbo-split">
					<div class="fsbo-stat reveal">
						<div class="vs"><span class="big agent">$435,000</span><span class="word">with an agent</span></div>
						<div class="vs" style="margin-top:10px"><span class="big">$380,000</span><span class="word">on your own</span></div>
						<p class="cap">Median sale prices, agent-assisted versus for-sale-by-owner
							(National Association of Realtors, 2024 Profile of Home Buyers and Sellers).</p>
						<p class="share">FSBO has fallen from <strong>21% of home sales in 1985</strong> to a
							record-low <strong>6% in 2024</strong>.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="fsbo-rows reveal">
						<div class="fsbo-row">
							<h3>Pricing</h3>
							<p>17% of FSBO sellers called getting the price right their hardest task (NAR, 2024), and 64%
								of sellers who went solo said they did not get their desired price (Clever Real Estate FSBO survey).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="fsbo-row">
							<h3>Paperwork</h3>
							<p>Understanding and performing the paperwork ranked among FSBO sellers' hardest steps
								(NAR, 2024). In the Clever survey, 43% of unrepresented sellers admitted to making legal mistakes.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="fsbo-row">
							<h3>Exposure</h3>
							<p>63% of FSBO sellers did not actively market their home at all (NAR, 2024). No campaign,
								no MLS push, no buyer pool beyond the sign in the yard.</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fsbo-close reveal">
					<p>A consultation costs nothing and commits you to nothing. You keep the pricing data either way.</p>
					<a class="btn" href="/contact-us/">Schedule a Consultation</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

